<exact compact JSON bytes of examples/02-delivery-direct.json>

# Receiver answers:
#   2xx                      accepted (transport receipt). Hub records receipt state=accepted by=hub.
#   408 / 429 / 5xx / net    retried: min(1h, 2^attempt s) + jitter, Retry-After honoured, 8 attempts, then dead_letter.
#   409                      identity conflict (same webhook-id, different bytes): terminal, operator alerted.
#   410 / 413 / other 4xx    terminal: receipt state=failed, then dead_letter.
# Retries resend identical bytes and webhook-id; only webhook-timestamp, webhook-signature and X-Vecnet-Attempt change.
# Before a push route goes live the hub sends {"type":"verification","challenge":"<43 chars base64url>"} and the receiver echoes {"challenge":"<same>"}.
